comments.message:
Is it worth doing something to get rid of these?

In file `tests/vitest.setup.js`:

```
// Import the mock component
import SvgStub from './SvgStub';
import { vi } from 'vitest';

// Mock all SVG imports globally
vi.mock('*.svg', () => ({
  default: SvgStub,
}));
```

Stole this idea, half-baked

As I understand `globals: true` means you don't need any import. So I was surprised to see this setting `globals: true` and the imports still in the tests: 
`import { vi, describe, it, expect } from 'vitest'`;

Maybe we can set globals: false like the default ?

Acknowledged. Then I would think the imports like 

import { vi, describe, it, expect } from 'vitest';


Aren't needed? But oh well, I am good. Maybe easier if we try one day to disable globals
